WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:15.089
This week I spent a few nights at the Sydney Capsule Hotel.

00:00:15.089 --> 00:00:20.069
I was in town for a physics conference, and I thought it would set the mood nicely.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:54.570
There are about 16 pods in the room, each with their own storage locker.

00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:55.398
My initial impression is that it's really good, but it's getting late and

00:01:55.399 --> 00:02:01.218
I don't want to disturb the people around me so to avoid this from becoming a capsule hotel

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:04.039
ASMR, I'll talk to you tomorrow.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.060
Open the pod bay doors Hal.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:26.130
Hey, so here's my review so far...

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:29.160
It's definitely very futuristic,

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:36.209
it has vibes of hibernating on a spaceship on our on our way to a destination somewhere and

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:43.949
it's pretty spacious actually. There is room to move around if you consider this to be room.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:46.619
It's about one meter by two meters.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:53.819
It's pretty much like a backpackers though when you take away all the futuristic stuff.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:57.479
It's kind of in between a backpackers and a hotel.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:05.369
You've got a lot more privacy than a normal backpackers, and the price is about in between the two of them as well,

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:13.440
maybe $50 or $60 a night. It kind of feels a little bit antisocial because you never really see your neighbors

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:20.099
and it kind of feels like everyone just keeps to their own pod probably on their phones or whatever.

00:03:20.769 --> 00:03:27.569
It's nice in that way, but it can also feel a little bit lonely in here. Having said that everyone

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:30.029
i've met so far has been really friendly here

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:35.640
and I think it's because a lot of people are here for the novel experience, and they want to try it out.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:42.869
Something that I do like about being in this capsule is that it makes the world feel small

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:50.910
so it's a real contrast between the bustling streets of Sydney down below because we're right in the center of the city and

00:03:51.459 --> 00:03:53.819
being in your own little pod where

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:56.519
you're sort of removed from all of that.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:04.049
And I kind of like that feeling, I feel like it's almost easy to be creative inside of the pod

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:09.690
because it sort of removes distractions, and you're left with just the white

00:04:10.269 --> 00:04:12.989
electronic style walls and your own mind.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:18.810
There are definitely some downsides to it, like the pods themselves are actually

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:26.489
really quite flimsy. They seem to be made out of some sort of plastic material and that means that you can feel

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:31.479
other people in their pods sort of moving around or when they get in and out and

00:04:32.539 --> 00:04:38.109
if you're really sensitive to sort of disturbances at night, maybe you wouldn't get a very good sleep.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.979
I found it okay

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:47.079
but definitely you can hear other people and whilst everyone has been really respectful and not made much noise,

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:52.809
it's definitely a sense of not being totally isolated.

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:22.030
The capsules themselves don't make any noise. The inbuilt alarm wakes you up with flashing lights

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:24.310
which was a bit startling.

00:05:25.039 --> 00:05:30.098
There is a TV - but it doesn't display instructions in English

00:05:30.139 --> 00:05:33.158
and it was pretty hard to use to be honest

